2025-07-29 22:03:20 - src.vue_api_endpoints - INFO - JSON data received: {'text': "\n--- Page 1 ---\nSTATEMEMENT OF ADDITIONAL AUTHORITIES  \nLAW OFFICES OF LISE ELLNER \nPOST OFFICE BOX 2711 \nVASHON, WA 98070 \nTEL (206) 930-1090 \nFax (206) 463-0758 \nIN THE SUPREME COURT OF THE STATE OF \nWASHINGTON \n \nSTATE OF WASHINGTON, ) \n \n \n \n \n \n) \n \n \nRespondent, \n) \nS. CT. 999414 \n \n \n \n \n \n)           \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n) \n \n \n \n \n \n) \n                 V. \n \n \n) \nSTATEMENT OF  \n \n \n \n \n \n) \nADDITIONAL \n) \nAUTHORITIES. RAP   \n) \n10.8 \n) \n \nROBERT AYERST \n          ) \n \n \nAppellant.        ) \nJUSTIN LEWIS, \n          ) \n \nAppellant         ) \n_____________________________  ) \n \n \nThe following are offered as additional authority: \n Gonzalez–Lopez, 548 U.S. 140, 150–51, 126 S.Ct. 2557, \n165 L.Ed.2d 409 (2006) This is a counsel of choice case \nexplaining  the right to counsel  “derives from the root \nmeaning of the constitutional  guarantee.” It does not \ndepend on  the quality or skill level of counsel-which is \ndifferent from Ineffective assistance of counsel cases. \n \nEx Parte Garland, 71 U.S. 333, 32 How. Pr 214, 18 L.Ed. \n366, 4 Wall. 333 (1986) recognizes the states alone \nFILED \nSUPREME COURT \nSTATE OF WASHINGTON \n5/23/2022 10:34 AM \nBY ERIN L. LENNON \nCLERK \n\n--- Page 2 ---\nSTATEMEMENT OF ADDITIONAL AUTHORITIES  \nLAW OFFICES OF LISE ELLNER \nPOST OFFICE BOX 2711 \nVASHON, WA 98070 \nTEL (206) 930-1090 \nFax (206) 463-0758 \nsubject to  due process, determine who meets the \nqualifications to be considered counsel.  \n \nIn re Bruen, 102 Wash. 472, 172 P.1152 (1918) cited Ex \nParte Garland for the exclusive constitutional authority to \ndetermine who is counsel.  \n \nUnited States v. Nixon, 418 U.S. 683, 94 S.Ct. 3090, \n3096, 41 L.Ed.2d 1039 (1974), quoting Marbury v. \nMadison, 5 U.S. 137, 1 Cranch 137, 177, 2 L.Ed. 60 \n(1803), “[i]t is emphatically the province and duty of the \njudicial department to say what the law is.”  \n \nShort v. Demopolis, 103 Wn.2d 52, 62, 691 P.3d 163 \n(1984) This Court has sole authority under art 4 sec. 1 to \nsafeguard the right to counsel under  art. 1. Sec. 3, 22, \nand the 6th Amend. to protect the individual clients, the \ncourt, the proper administration of justice, the dignity and \npurity of the profession, and for the public good.”  \n \n \n \nDATED this 23rd day of May 2022. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nRespectfully \nsubmitted, \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nLISE ELLNER \n\n--- Page 3 ---\nSTATEMEMENT OF ADDITIONAL AUTHORITIES  \nLAW OFFICES OF LISE ELLNER \nPOST OFFICE BOX 2711 \nVASHON, WA 98070 \nTEL (206) 930-1090 \nFax (206) 463-0758 \n \n \nWSBA No. 20955 \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAttorney for Appellant \n \n \nI Lise Ellner, person over the age of 18 years old, served \nthe \nAsotin \nCounty \nProsecutor’s \nOffice \nbnichols@co.asotin.wa.us \nand \nGideon \nNewmark \n<gideon.newmark@opd.wa.gov>; 'Boruchowitz, Robert' \n<boruchor@seattleu.edu>; \n'Even, \nJeffrey \nT \n(ATG)' \n<jeffrey.even@atg.wa.gov>; \n'John \nMidgley' \n<jmidgley@aclu-wa.org> Nancy Talner <TALNER@aclu-\nwa.org> a true copy of the document to which this \ncertificate is affixed on May 23, 2022. Service was made \nby electronically to all parties \n \n \n \nI, Lise Ellnr, certify the word count is 227 in compliance \nwith RAP 17.18 \n\n--- Page 4 ---\nLAW OFFICES OF LISE ELLNER\nMay 23, 2022 - 10:34 AM\nTransmittal Information\nFiled with Court:\nSupreme Court\nAppellate Court Case Number:   99941-4\nAppellate Court Case Title:\nPersonal Restraint Petition of Robert L. Ayerst\nSuperior Court Case Number:\n16-1-00150-7\nThe following documents have been uploaded:\n999414_State_of_Add_Authorities_20220523103105SC276674_0633.pdf \n    This File Contains: \n     Statement of Additional Authorities \n     The Original File Name was Additional AuthoritiesSupremes.pdf\nA copy of the uploaded files will be sent to:\nJYoung@co.asotin.wa.us\nbnichols@co.asotin.wa.us\nboruchor@seattleu.edu\ncliedkie@co.asotin.wa.us\njaimehawk@hotmail.com\njeffrey.even@atg.wa.gov\njhawk@aclu-wa.org\njmidgley@aclu-wa.org\npleadings@aclu-wa.org\nrcboru@aol.com\nsgoolyef@atg.wa.gov\ntalner@aclu-wa.org\nComments:\nSender Name: Lise Ellner - Email: liseellnerlaw@comcast.net \nAddress: \nPO BOX 2711 \nVASHON, WA, 98070-2711 \nPhone: 206-930-1090\nNote: The Filing Id is 20220523103105SC276674\n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n• \n", 'source': 'text_input'}
